{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing ll = long long;\nusing pii = pair<ll, int>;\n\nconst int MX = 5500;\nconst ll INF = 1000000007LL;\n\nint n, m, k, c, d;\nint s = MX - 2, t = MX - 1;\nint mf = 0;\nll ans = 0;\nll dist[MX];\nint parent_edge[MX];\n\nstruct Edge {\n    int to, cost, rev_idx, capacity;\n};\n\nvector<Edge> graph[MX];\n\nvoid add_edge(int u, int v, int cost, int capacity) {\n    int sz_u = graph[u].size();\n    int sz_v = graph[v].size();\n    graph[u].push_back({v, cost, sz_v, capacity});\n    graph[v].push_back({u, -cost, sz_u, 0});\n}\n\nvoid dijkstra() {\n    fill(dist, dist + MX, INF);\n    priority_queue<pii, vector<pii>, greater<pii>> pq;\n    dist[s] = 0;\n    pq.push({0, s});\n    \n    while (!pq.empty()) {\n        auto [d_val, u] = pq.top();\n        pq.pop();\n        if (d_val > dist[u]) continue;\n        \n        for (const auto& e : graph[u]) {\n            if (e.capacity > 0 && dist[e.to] > d_val + e.cost) {\n                dist[e.to] = d_val + e.cost;\n                parent_edge[e.to] = e.rev_idx;\n                pq.push({dist[e.to], e.to});\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nvoid augment() {\n    int flow = k;\n    int cur = t;\n    while (cur != s) {\n        int prev = graph[cur][parent_edge[cur]].to;\n        int idx = graph[cur][parent_edge[cur]].rev_idx;\n        flow = min(flow, graph[prev][idx].capacity);\n        cur = prev;\n    }\n    \n    mf += flow;\n    ans += flow * dist[t];\n    \n    cur = t;\n    while (cur != s) {\n        int prev = graph[cur][parent_edge[cur]].to;\n        int idx = graph[cur][parent_edge[cur]].rev_idx;\n        graph[cur][parent_edge[cur]].capacity += flow;\n        graph[prev][idx].capacity -= flow;\n        cur = prev;\n    }\n}\n\nint node(int u, int time) {\n    return u + time * n;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    cin >> n >> m >> k >> c >> d;\n    int max_time = n + k;\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < k; ++i) {\n        cin >> u;\n        add_edge(s, node(u, 0), 0, 1);\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i <= max_time; ++i) {\n        add_edge(node(1, i), t, 1LL * c * i, k);\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < max_time; ++j) {\n            add_edge(node(i, j), node(i, j + 1), 0, k);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    while (m--) {\n        cin >> u >> v;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= k; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < max_time; ++j) {\n                int cost = d * (2 * i - 1);\n                add_edge(node(u, j), node(v, j + 1), cost, 1);\n                add_edge(node(v, j), node(u, j + 1), cost, 1);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    while (mf < k) {\n        dijkstra();\n        augment();\n    }\n    \n    cout << ans;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int MX = 5500;\n    static final long INF = 1000000007L;\n\n    static int n, m, k, c, d;\n    static int s = MX - 2, t = MX - 1;\n    static int mf = 0;\n    static long ans = 0;\n    static long[] dist = new long[MX];\n    static int[] parent_edge = new int[MX];\n\n    static class Edge {\n        int to, cost, rev_idx, capacity;\n\n        Edge(int to, int cost, int rev_idx, int capacity) {\n            this.to = to;\n            this.cost = cost;\n            this.rev_idx = rev_idx;\n            this.capacity = capacity;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static List<Edge>[] graph = new List[MX];\n\n    static void add_edge(int u, int v, int cost, int capacity) {\n        int sz_u = graph[u].size();\n        int sz_v = graph[v].size();\n        graph[u].add(new Edge(v, cost, sz_v, capacity));\n        graph[v].add(new Edge(u, -cost, sz_u, 0));\n    }\n\n    static void dijkstra() {\n        Arrays.fill(dist, INF);\n        PriorityQueue<int[]> pq = new PriorityQueue<>(Comparator.comparingInt(a -> a[0]));\n        dist[s] = 0;\n        pq.offer(new int[]{0, s});\n\n        while (!pq.isEmpty()) {\n            int[] top = pq.poll();\n            int d_val = top[0], u = top[1];\n            if (d_val > dist[u]) continue;\n\n            for (Edge e : graph[u]) {\n                if (e.capacity > 0 && dist[e.to] > d_val + e.cost) {\n                    dist[e.to] = d_val + e.cost;\n                    parent_edge[e.to] = e.rev_idx;\n                    pq.offer(new int[]{(int) dist[e.to], e.to});\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    static void augment() {\n        int flow = k;\n        int cur = t;\n        while (cur != s) {\n            int prev = graph[cur].get(parent_edge[cur]).to;\n            int idx = graph[cur].get(parent_edge[cur]).rev_idx;\n            flow = Math.min(flow, graph[prev].get(idx).capacity);\n            cur = prev;\n        }\n\n        mf += flow;\n        ans += (long) flow * dist[t];\n\n        cur = t;\n        while (cur != s) {\n            int prev = graph[cur].get(parent_edge[cur]).to;\n            int idx = graph[cur].get(parent_edge[cur]).rev_idx;\n            graph[cur].get(parent_edge[cur]).capacity += flow;\n            graph[prev].get(idx).capacity -= flow;\n            cur = prev;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static int node(int u, int time) {\n        return u + time * n;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        n = sc.nextInt();\n        m = sc.nextInt();\n        k = sc.nextInt();\n        c = sc.nextInt();\n        d = sc.nextInt();\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < MX; i++) {\n            graph[i] = new ArrayList<>();\n        }\n\n        int max_time = n + k;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < k; ++i) {\n            int u = sc.nextInt();\n            add_edge(s, node(u, 0), 0, 1);\n        }\n\n        for (int i = 0; i <= max_time; ++i) {\n            add_edge(node(1, i), t, (int) (1L * c * i), k);\n        }\n\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < max_time; ++j) {\n                add_edge(node(i, j), node(i, j + 1), 0, k);\n            }\n        }\n\n        while (m-- > 0) {\n            int u = sc.nextInt();\n            int v = sc.nextInt();\n            for (int i = 1; i <= k; ++i) {\n                for (int j = 0; j < max_time; ++j) {\n                    int cost = d * (2 * i - 1);\n                    add_edge(node(u, j), node(v, j + 1), cost, 1);\n                    add_edge(node(v, j), node(u, j + 1), cost, 1);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        while (mf < k) {\n            dijkstra();\n            augment();\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00034374051028862596, -2.622600959512056e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.0015570909017696977, -7.64102369430475e-05, -0.06197310611605644, -0.038126446306705475, -1.9907753085135482e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -7.009260298218578e-05, -0.0028055852744728327, -5.8410845667822286e-05, -0.0